DEBUG: Processing VERI-1976
The error message VERI-1976 appears when a sampled value system function is
passed a clocking argument that is not a clocking event. According to IEEE
1800-2017 LRM, Section 16.9.3, the value of the expression argument is sampled
in the clocking event argument, which must be an event control expression
preceded by "@".

Example:
    # property.v
    property p(sig, clk);
        @(clk) $changed(sig, clk);
    endproperty

    # run.tcl
    % analyze -sv property.v

    [ERROR (VERI-1976)] property.v(2): clocking argument for changed is not of type event control

NOTE:
This message does not appear if an event control expression is passed as
argument, for example:

    # property.v
    property p(sig, clk);
        @(clk) $changed(sig, @(posedge clk));
    endproperty

    # run.tcl
    % analyze -sv property.v

    (No errors)

